# T6 handover patch — Godot 4.6 CowData header (docs/analysis.md §17.1)
#
# Godot 4.6 inserts a `capacity` field into the CowData header and aligns the payload to
# Memory::MAX_ALIGN (16 on the official Windows toolchain), so the element count moves from
# buffer-0x8 to buffer-0x10. The calibrator hardcodes buffer-0x8 in two places; with it, a 4.6
# target decodes NO string at all and the run reports "found no StringName slot for RootHarness".
#
# This patch does not gate on a version. It DERIVES the distance from raw byte-scan hits for two
# anchor names of different lengths, and refuses rather than guessing when the answer is ambiguous.
# On 4.3/4.4.1/4.5 it derives -0x8 and changes nothing measurable; on 4.6.3 it derives -0x10.
#
# NOT APPLIED IN-TREE: src/Godot.External.Calibrator/ was owned by concurrent work (T2/T3) when this
# was written, so it was developed and run against a private copy of that project. Every 4.6 number
# in docs/analysis.md §17 came from a driver built from the patched copy.
#
#   apply with:  git apply docs/t6-cowdata-4.6.patch     (from the repository root)
#
# Verified: 3 full-grid passes, 16 cells, one frozen driver. The four 4.6.3 cells go from deriving
# nothing to 11/12 clean cell-runs; the 4.3/4.4.1/4.5 cells are unchanged against a same-machine
# baseline run with the unpatched driver.

